    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2216" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰγυπτι-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be like an Egyptian</i>, i.e. <i>to be sly and
				crafty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				378
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				922
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>speak Egyptian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Philops.</u>
				31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be like Egypt</i>, i.e. <i>be under water</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.14
			</span></i>.</div>
